  "id": "NSWG-COR-41",
  "summary": "Guard against response-splitting of HTTP trailing headers added via\n[`response.addTrailers()`](https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_response_addtrailers_headers)\nby removing new-line (`[\\r\\n]`) characters from values. Note that standard\nheader values are already stripped of new-line characters. The expected security\nimpact is low because trailing headers are rarely used.\n\n",
